---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
---
<Shell
  current="mesh"
  title="Mesh — relay topology · The Grid"
  description="The MeshCore mesh as a topology map: every located node (colored by role) with the relay links reconstructed from each advert's path — the repeater chain it traversed, resolved to mapped nodes. Built from GET /api/v1/events?layer=mesh."
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/lib/maplibre-gl.css" />
    <style is:global>
      .mesh-topbar { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 8px 18px; margin: 20px 0 12px; }
      #mesh-stats { font-size: 13.5px; }
      /* The window control is a .pill group (app.css §6) — mesh.js builds it. */
      #mesh-window { display: inline-flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; }
      #mesh-legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 14px; margin-left: auto; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-2nd); }
      .mesh-leg { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
      /* The one place a radius survives, and deliberately: these are the map's
         node dots repeated as a key, and a node is drawn as a circle. */
      .mesh-dot { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; display: inline-block; border: 1px solid var(--ink); }
      #mesh-canvas {
        width: 100%; height: 620px; border: 1px solid var(--ink);
        background: var(--paper-sunken); position: relative; overflow: hidden;
      }
      /* Popup: a paper surface over the light basemap, mirroring the map page —
         no radius, no drop shadow, and the paper severity ramp it inherits. */
      .maplibregl-popup-content {
        background: var(--paper); color: var(--text-body); border: 1px solid var(--ink);
        font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; padding: 10px 12px; box-shadow: none;
      }
      .maplibregl-popup-close-button { color: var(--text-muted-p); font-size: 17px; }
      .map-popup .popup-headline { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 5px; }
      .map-popup .popup-chips { margin-bottom: 6px; }
      .mesh-roletag { font-weight: 600; }
      .popup-details-dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 2px 12px; margin: 0; }
      .popup-details-dl dt { color: var(--text-tertiary); font-size: 11px; }
      .popup-details-dl dd { margin: 0; color: var(--text-body); font-size: 12px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
      @media (max-width: 720px) { #mesh-canvas { height: 66vh; } #mesh-legend { margin-left: 0; } }
    </style>
  </Fragment>

  <PageHead kicker="Relay topology" title="Mesh">
    <p class="lead">The MeshCore mesh as a topology map.</p>
  </PageHead>

  <p class="rail-caption">
    <b>Nodes</b><code class="inline">/api/v1/events?layer=mesh</code>, colored by role ·
    <b>links</b><code class="inline">/api/v1/mesh/links</code>, each advert's relay path rolled up
    into a durable weighted edge list — links fade by recency (a quiet-but-recent link is dim, not
    gone) and thicken with traffic, and the window trades currency for history · coverage is
    deliberately wide, Bay Area → Sierra ·
    <strong class="accent-orange">a sparse map is not an all-clear — a node is drawn only once we
    have heard it advertise a location</strong>
  </p>

  <div class="mesh-topbar">
    <div id="mesh-stats" class="muted">Loading the mesh…</div>
    <div id="mesh-window" aria-label="Time window"></div>
    <div id="mesh-legend"></div>
  </div>

  <div id="mesh-canvas"></div>
  <div id="mesh-errors" class="section-gap"></div>

  <!-- The node roster. The map answers "where is the mesh"; this answers "what
       exactly did we hear, and how long ago" — including nodes whose telemetry
       is partial, which a map dot cannot express. -->
  <div class="section-gap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="left"><h2>Nodes heard</h2></div>
      <span class="cap">node · type · snr / rssi · hops · heard</span>
    </div>
    <div class="with-rail">
      <div class="rail-main">
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table class="data-table capped-head">
            <thead>
              <!-- No width hints: with .capped-head the header is taken out of
                   flow, so th widths no longer size the columns. The cells
                   carry their own units ("9 dB", "2 hops", "5 min ago") and
                   size themselves. -->
              <tr>
                <th>Node</th><th>Type</th><th>SNR / RSSI</th>
                <th class="num">Hops</th><th>Heard</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="mesh-tbody"><tr><td colspan="5"><span class="loading">Loading nodes…</span></td></tr></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="page-rail" aria-label="How to read the roster">
        <div class="rail-block">
          <div class="rail-label">Ambient state</div>
          <p>
            Mesh presence is <code class="inline">INFO</code>: excluded from a place's
            <code class="inline">totalActive</code>, its severity counts, its top events and its
            area mode. A busy mesh does not raise an alert level, and a quiet one does not lower
            it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rail-block">
          <div class="rail-label">Telemetry is volatile</div>
          <p>
            SNR, RSSI and hop count are deliberately excluded from the content hash, so they never
            mint a revision — only a node's identity, location or status does.
          </p>
          <p>Missing telemetry renders as <span class="mono">—</span>, never <span class="mono">0</span>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rail-block">
          <div class="rail-label alert">Which clock</div>
          <p>
            To ask when a node last spoke, read the event's
            <code class="inline">observedAt</code> — not
            <code class="inline">telemetry.lastAdvertAt</code>, which the node stamps from its own
            unsynchronized clock.
          </p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script is:inline src="/lib/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
  <script is:inline type="module">
    import { initMeshPage } from '/assets/pages/mesh.js';
    initMeshPage();
  </script>
</Shell>
